@startuml controlled-restart
!theme plain
' Updated: accepted architecture-review findings (2026-10-13)
title Controlled restart: persisted fence -> drain -> park -> confirmed absence -> eligibility -> start -> reconcile -> release (contracts/restart-and-takeover.md)

actor "Operator" as Op
participant "Session host\n(M1 supervisor)" as SH
database "Host store\n(fences, inbox, journal)" as HS
participant "Context Engine\n(M2, host package)" as CE
participant "Holder +\nold harness" as H1
participant "Bridge\n(M3)" as BR
participant "Composer\n(curator-run)" as C
database "B1 Task store\n(board sessions)" as B1
participant "Fresh agent-side runner +\nnew harness" as H2
participant "Launch dispatcher" as D
participant "User manager / launcher" as UM

Op -> SH: restart(session, controlled), signed control envelope
SH -> SH: admit(control.restart): grant, target, fence state
SH -> HS: fence.close(op_id, reason=restart), fsync
note right of HS
  Serialized with start, wake, retry, probe.
  Enqueue still persists (queued);
  nothing is dispatched while closed.
end note

== Drain ==
SH -> CE: stop dispatch; wait for turn boundary
CE -> CE: void pending interactions
SH -> SH: process group has no tool children?\nexternal effects settled? (kernel locks, build lock, CR ops)
alt drain timeout or effect still in flight
  SH --> Op: restart_aborted{drain}; old execution keeps running;\nfence stays closed until the operator decides
else drained
  == Park ==
  CE -> H1: host notice: write a park note (swarm-tail park)
  alt note in time
    H1 -> BR: swarm-tail park "<note>" (agent_authored)
    BR -> CE: park note via typed API
  else timeout
    CE -> CE: summary from the journal
  end
  CE -> HS: HandoffPackage (swarm-handoff/2) at watermark H
  opt board session
    SH -> B1: commit goal revision with handoff_ref (CAS)
    B1 --> SH: committed revision (ready evidence)
  end

  == Stop with confirmed absence ==
  SH -> D: host_stop under session-scoped permit
  D -> UM: journaled E-stop: exec.stop with latest execution receipt
  UM -> UM: account-wide generation-UID stop and quiet-period absence;\nincluding escaped and OS-spawned processes (user manager §4.7)
  UM --> D: authoritative process-absence result (no native-lock proof)
  D --> SH: stop result; same-effect recovery on unknown
  note over SH, D: Unknown retains fence, claim and capacity; no host-owned signals
  alt absence not confirmed
    SH --> Op: stop_unconfirmed; no replacement; fence stays closed
  else absent
    == Eligibility ==
    SH -> C: compare-only (profile_pin, fragment digest, system-modules)
    C --> SH: current digests (no plan)
    SH -> SH: compare stored plan pins, effective posture,\nbinding rev, grants, auth readiness, approved artifact, ordinary startup qualification;\nD-RESUME semver; R-STANDING surface digests
    alt any mismatch or failure
      SH -> HS: session state parked_refused{reason}; fence stays closed
      SH --> Op: refused{reason}. Path ends: no rebind, no delivery.\nAccepting drift is a new operation that rebuilds
    else eligible
      SH -> D: successor host_start under owner session lifecycle authorisation\nand session permit; previous claim confirmed absent
      D -> D: per-start claim (execution_id, controller_epoch, op_id);\ncurrent authority and receipt interlock (dispatcher §12)
      D -> UM: invoke privileged launcher; stored immutable plan
      UM -> H2: fresh runner under agent UID; new execution-local generation
      H2 -> SH: current-epoch registration via jointly gated channel\n(proof unpublished; session host §3.3)
      H2 -> H2: check native-lock absence under closed fence;\nseparate from process absence
      break native lock unknown or held
        H2 --> SH: park; delivery stays closed; no harness initialisation/resume
      end
      SH -> CE: initialize native resume (same machine, home, pin, transcript, transport)
      CE -> H2: native resume; same major, same minor for 0.x\n(no extra version-change probe; per-harness semver exception note)
      CE -> H2: readiness probe
      alt init or readiness fails
        SH -> D: compensate via host_stop and account-wide absence
        SH --> Op: resume-failed if harness resume failed; caller decides;\nno automatic/portable-seed fallback; fence stays closed
      else ready
        SH -> CE: reconcile input markers: applied resolves without replay;\nconfirmed non-application permits only eligible ordinary-input retry;\nunresolved stays unknown; unknown approvals/control never auto-replay
        break unresolved application evidence
          SH --> Op: unknown; delivery stays closed; status/authorised stop reachable
        end
        SH -> HS: fence.open(op_id) only after registration, readiness and reconciliation, fsync
        CE -> H2: dispatch queued items in order
        CE -> BR: receipts dispatched / applied
        SH --> Op: restart report (op_id, handoff_ref, applied, pending, unknown)
      end
    end
  end
end
@enduml
